# Purpose

The primary purpose of this project is to build a simple java application that bridges
different types of transport protocols together, so that applications
can communicate binary data even when they don't support matching protocol types.

A secondary purpose is to create a form of protocol diode, in which one-way
forwarding rules will allow some applications to have full-duplex connectivity
to an application, without the other application having full duplex connection
back. This can be useful when you'd like have a one-way monitoring connection
between two networks, with the guarantee that data can't flow backwards
across the connection.

Finally, this allows for websocket connections to be bridged down to traditional
TCP connections or UDP connections, so that systems which are only coded to
talk using traditional transport protocols can still exchange data with browser
clients via the transport of binary websocket frames.